msgid "‘Ali was told to stay behind until he had returned the deposits people had left with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "An umarci Aliyu da ya zauna a baya har sai ya mayar da amanonin da mutane suka ajiye a wurin Annabi ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers came so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Masu neman sun matso kusa sosai har Abu Bakr ya raɗa da cewa, “Idan ɗayansu ya duba ƙarƙashin ƙafafunsa, zai gan mu.” Annabi ﷺ ya amsa masa da cewa, “Me kake tsammani game da mutum biyu da Allah ne na ukunsu?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah recalled this moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Allah Ya ambaci wannan lokaci a cikin Alƙur'ani: “na biyun biyu, a lokacin da suke cikin kogon, yayin da yake cewa da abokinsa, ‘Kada ka yi baƙin ciki; lallai Allah Yana tare da mu.’”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Ibn Ishaq’s telling, when the three nights had passed, Asma brought their food but had no strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and tied it on, and so she was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "A labarin Ibn Ishaq, bayan darare ukun sun shuɗe, Asma ta kawo musu abinci amma ba ta da madaurin da za ta rataye jakar da shi. Sai ta kwance ɗamararta ta ɗaure shi da ita, shi ya sa aka kira ta Mai Ɗamaru Biyu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The pursuers climbed the mountain and passed the cave. Seeing a spider’s web across its opening, they said no one could have gone in there, and moved on. Ibn Kathir calls this report’s chain good."
msgstr "Masu bin sahun sun haura dutsen suka wuce ta bakin kogon. Da suka ga saƙar gizo-gizo a ƙofarsa, suka ce babu yadda za a yi wani ya shiga ciki, sai suka wuce. Ibn Kathir ya ce isnadin wannan ruwaya yana da kyau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Some tell that the searchers saw a spider’s web across the cave’s opening, and walked on."
msgstr "Wasu sun ruwaito cewa masu neman sun ga saƙar gizo-gizo a bakin kogon, sai suka wuce gaba."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari gives three nights. Which nights of the week they were comes from a later biography."
msgstr "Al-Bukhari ya ambaci darare uku. Ko wane darare ne a cikin mako kuma ya fito ne daga wani littafin tarihin rayuwa na gaba."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how the two reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid there for three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta ba da labarin yadda su biyun suka isa wani kogo a Dutsen Thawr suka ɓoye a can na tsawon darare uku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how her brother ‘Abdullah spent the nights with them and brought them news from Makkah after dark."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta ba da labarin yadda ɗan’uwanta ‘Abdullah ya riƙa kwana tare da su yana kawo musu labarai daga Makkah da zarar dare ya yi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought the ewes to the cave each evening of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta ba da labarin yadda ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah ya riƙa kai tumakin zuwa kogon a kowace yammacin dararen ukun."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr recalls fearing that anyone who looked down at his own feet would see them."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ya tuna yadda ya ji tsoron cewa duk wanda ya duba ƙarƙashin ƙafafunsa zai gan su."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The verse speaks of the Prophet ﷺ as the second of two in the cave, telling his companion not to grieve."
msgstr "Ayar ta ambaci Annabi ﷺ a matsayin na biyun biyu a cikin kogon, yana gaya wa abokinsa kada ya yi baƙin ciki."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir explains the verse: Allah supported and aided His Messenger, who sheltered in the cave for three days."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir ya yi bayanin ayar: Allah Ya goyi bayan Manzonsa kuma Ya taimake shi, wanda ya fake a cikin kogon na tsawon kwanaki uku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how Asma tied the food bag with her waist-belt, and so was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya ba da labarin yadda Asma ta ɗaure jakar abincin da ɗamararta, shi ya sa aka kira ta Mai Ɗamaru Biyu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The report of the spider’s web across the cave’s opening, whose chain Ibn Kathir calls good."
msgstr "Ruwayar game da saƙar gizo-gizo a bakin kogon, wadda Ibn Kathir ya ce isnadinta yana da kyau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A modern biography names the three nights: the nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday."
msgstr "Wani littafin tarihin rayuwa na zamani ya ambaci dararen ukun: dararen da suka gabaci Juma'a, Asabar da Lahadi."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "The number beside each book counts its source passages."
msgstr "Lambar da ke gefen kowane littafi ita ce yawan nassoshin madogararsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid inside it. They would stay there for three nights."
msgstr "Annabin ﷺ da Abu Bakr sun isa wani kogo a Dutsen Thawr suka ɓuya a ciki. Za su kwashe darare uku a wurin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each night, Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah slept near them. Before dawn he slipped back to Makkah, so that morning found him among Quraysh as if he had never left, and at dark he returned with any plot he had heard."
msgstr "A kowane dare, ɗan Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, yakan kwana kusa da su. Kafin alfijir yakan lallaɓa ya koma Makkah, ta yadda gari na wayewa yana tare da Quraysh kamar bai taɓa fita ba, idan kuma dare ya yi yakan dawo musu da duk wata makarkashiya da ya ji."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah grazed a few milking ewes nearby and brought them to the cave after nightfall, so the two had milk. He did this on each of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Yantaccen bawan Abu Bakr, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, ya riƙa kiwon wasu ƴan tumaki masu nono a kusa da wurin, sannan ya kawo su kogon da zarar dare ya yi domin su biyun su sami nono. Ya yi hakan a kowane ɗaya daga cikin dararen guda uku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr slipped into a cave on Mount Thawr and stayed out of sight. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Annabi ﷺ da Abu Bakr sun kutsa cikin wani kogo a Dutsen Thawr suka ɓuya. Tsawon dare uku, kogon ne mafakarsu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They were not alone for long. Each night Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah came after dark with whatever Quraysh were plotting, then slipped back before dawn, so that morning found him in Makkah as if he had never left."
msgstr "Ba su daɗe su kaɗai ba. Kowace dare, ɗan Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, yakan zo bayan dare ya kawo musu duk abin da Quraysh ke ƙulla wa, sa’an nan ya koma a ɓoye kafin ketowar alfijir. Da safe, sai a gan shi a Makkah kamar bai taɓa barin wurin ba."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "And as darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought a few milking ewes to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. Every one of the three nights, he came."
msgstr "Sa’ad da duhu ya mamaye, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, wanda Abu Bakr ya ’yanta, yakan kawo wasu ’yan tumaki masu nono zuwa kogon, domin su biyun su sha madara sabuwa. Ya zo a kowace dare daga cikin dararen ukun."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the searchers came close, so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Sai masu nema suka matso kusa, har Abu Bakr ya raɗa, “Da ɗayansu zai kalli ƙafafunsa, da ya gan mu.” Annabi ﷺ ya amsa, “Me kake gani game da mutum biyu, alhali Allah ne na uku tare da su?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah preserved that moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Allah Ya adana wannan lokaci a cikin Alƙur’ani: “na biyu daga cikin mutum biyu, a lokacin da suke cikin kogon, sa’ad da ya ce wa abokinsa, ‘Kada ka yi baƙin ciki; Allah yana tare da mu.’”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Late that night the Prophet ﷺ left his house and set out with Abu Bakr, who carried all his savings with him. They did not take the road north to Madinah, but turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "A ƙarshen wannan dare, Annabi ﷺ ya bar gidansa ya kama hanya tare da Abu Bakr, wanda ya ɗauki duk abin da ya tara na kuɗi. Ba su bi hanyar arewa zuwa Madinah ba; sai suka juya kudu, zuwa Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night, the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr quietly left Makkah. They went south, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "A wannan dare, Annabi ﷺ da Abu Bakr suka bar Makkah a ɓoye. Suka nufi kudu, akasin hanyar Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "About five miles on, they reached Mount Thawr. They climbed to a cave in its side and slipped inside, out of sight. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Bayan tafiyar kusan mil biyar, suka isa Dutsen Thawr. Suka hau zuwa wani kogo a gefensa, suka shiga ba tare da an gan su ba. Zai zama mafakarsu na dare uku."

