#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At al-‘Aqabah one pilgrimage season, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ recited the Quran to six men from Yathrib, who lived beside Jews. “By Allah,” they said to one another, “this is the prophet the Jews threatened you with.”"
msgstr "A lokacin aikin hajji a al-‘Aqabah, Annabi Muhammad ﷺ ya karanta Alƙur’ani ga wasu maza shida daga Yathrib, waɗanda suke zama kusa da Yahudawa. “Wallahi,” suka ce wa juna, “wannan ne annabin da Yahudawa suka yi muku barazana da shi.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One pilgrimage season, six men from the town of Yathrib listened to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, and believed."
msgstr "A wani lokacin aikin hajji, wasu maza shida daga garin Yathrib suka saurari Annabi Muhammad ﷺ, kuma suka yi imani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each year more came, until seventy-three men and two women met him there by night and pledged to protect him as they protected their own women and children. “I am of you and you are of me,” he said."
msgstr "A kowace shekara wasu sukan ƙara zuwa, har maza saba’in da uku da mata biyu suka haɗu da shi a can da dare, suka yi masa alƙawarin kāre shi kamar yadda suke kāre matansu da ’ya’yansu. “Ni daga cikinku nake, ku kuma daga gare ni kuke,” ya ce."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Later, many more came at night. They promised to keep him safe, just like their own families."
msgstr "Daga baya, wasu da yawa suka zo da dare. Suka yi alƙawarin kāre shi kamar yadda suke kāre iyalansu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "“It is Yathrib,” he told his companions, and group after group they slipped away to Madinah. At last, of those free to go, only he, Abu Bakr and ‘Ali were left. And he waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "“Yathrib ce,” ya gaya wa sahabbansa, kuma suka riƙa tafiya a ɓoye zuwa Madinah rukuni-rukuni. A ƙarshe, cikin waɗanda za su iya tafiya, shi da Abu Bakr da ‘Ali ne kawai suka rage. Ya kuma jira izinin Allah don ya bi su."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "So his friends moved to Yathrib, the town we call Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "Saboda haka, abokansa suka ƙaura zuwa Yathrib, garin da muke kira Madinah. Annabi ﷺ ya jira izinin Allah don ya bi su."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr asked again and again to go. “Do not hurry,” he was told. “Perhaps Allah will give you a companion.” So he waited, hoping it would be the Prophet ﷺ, and fed two camels for four months to have them ready."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ya riƙa neman izinin tafiya. Aka ce masa, “Kada ka yi gaggawa. Wataƙila Allah zai ba ka abokin tafiya.” Sai ya jira, yana fatan abokin tafiyar zai zama Annabi ﷺ, kuma ya ciyar da raƙuma biyu na tsawon watanni huɗu domin su kasance a shirye."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr wanted to go too. He was told to wait: perhaps Allah would give him a companion."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ma yana son tafiya. Aka ce masa ya jira: wataƙila Allah zai ba shi abokin tafiya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then one day, in the full heat of noon, the Prophet ﷺ came at an hour he never came, and said, “Allah has given me permission to leave.” “Companionship?” Abu Bakr asked. “Companionship.” And Abu Bakr wept for joy."
msgstr "Wata rana, a tsakiyar tsananin zafin rana, Annabi ﷺ ya zo a lokacin da bai saba zuwa ba, ya ce, “Allah ya ba ni izinin tafiya.” “Zan raka ka?” Abu Bakr ya tambaya. “Za ka raka ni.” Abu Bakr kuwa ya yi kuka don murna."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One hot noon, the Prophet ﷺ came with the news: they could go together! Abu Bakr cried for joy."
msgstr "A wani tsakar rana mai zafi, Annabi ﷺ ya zo da labari: za su iya tafiya tare! Abu Bakr ya yi kuka don murna."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hired a guide to bring the camels to the cave of Thawr after three nights. Abu Bakr’s daughter Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two, and became “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Suka ɗauki hayar jagora, wanda zai kai raƙuman zuwa kogon Thawr bayan dare uku. Asma, ’yar Abu Bakr, ba ta da abin ɗaure abincinsu, sai ta tsaga ɗamararta gida biyu, kuma ta zama “ma’abociyar ɗamaru biyu”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two and used that."
msgstr "Asma ba ta da abin ɗaure abincinsu, sai ta tsaga ɗamararta gida biyu ta yi amfani da su."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, Quraysh had watched his companions go, and feared he would follow. In Dar al-Nadwah their leaders took Abu Jahl’s plan: young men from every clan would strike him together, spreading his blood across them all."
msgstr "A Makkah, Quraysh sun ga sahabbansa suna tafiya, kuma suka ji tsoron zai bi su. A Dar al-Nadwah, shugabanninsu suka amince da shirin Abu Jahl: samari daga kowace ƙabila za su far masa tare, don laifin jininsa ya rataya a kan kowa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The leaders of Makkah were afraid of the Prophet ﷺ, and they made a plan to attack him."
msgstr "Shugabannin Makkah sun ji tsoron Annabi ﷺ, sai suka shirya su kai masa hari."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night the men gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak. “Sleep in it,” he said. “Nothing you dislike will reach you from them.”"
msgstr "A wannan dare, mutanen suka taru a ƙofar gidansa, suna jiran ya yi barci. Ya gaya wa ‘Ali ya kwanta a gadonsa, sanye da mayafinsa kore. Ya ce, “Ka kwanta a cikinsa. Ba abin da ba ka so zai same ka daga gare su.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. ‘Ali lay in the Prophet’s bed, wrapped in his green cloak."
msgstr "A wannan dare suka jira a wajen ƙofarsa. ‘Ali ya kwanta a gadon Annabi, sanye da mayafinsa kore."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then he came out to them with a handful of dust, scattering it over their heads and reciting, “So We have covered them, and they do not see.” Allah took their sight from him, and he went on his way."
msgstr "Sai ya fito gare su da tafin ƙasa, ya watsa musu ita a kawunansu, yana karanta, “Sai Muka rufe su, don haka ba sa gani.” Allah ya hana su ganinsa, sai ya kama hanyarsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ walked right out past them, scattering dust, and Allah kept them from seeing him."
msgstr "Annabi ﷺ ya wuce ta gabansu yana watsa ƙasa, kuma Allah ya hana su ganinsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came to Abu Bakr, and the two slipped out by a small door at the back of the house, Abu Bakr carrying all his savings. They did not take the road north to Madinah, but turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Ya je wurin Abu Bakr, sai su biyun suka fita a ɓoye ta wata ƙaramar ƙofa a bayan gida, Abu Bakr kuma yana ɗauke da duk abin da ya tara. Ba su bi hanyar arewa zuwa Madinah ba, sai suka nufi kudu, wajen Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He and his best friend, Abu Bakr, slipped away in the dark. They went south, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Shi da babban abokinsa Abu Bakr suka fita a ɓoye cikin duhu. Suka nufi kudu, akasin hanyar Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "About five miles on, they reached Mount Thawr and a cave in its side. Abu Bakr went in first, feeling his way in the dark, ready to take any harm himself. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Bayan sun yi tafiyar kusan mil biyar, suka isa Dutsen Thawr da wani kogo a gefensa. Abu Bakr ya shiga da farko, yana bincika hanyar a cikin duhu, a shirye ya fuskanci duk wani haɗari da kansa. Kogon zai zama maboyarsu na tsawon dare uku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They reached a cave on Mount Thawr. Abu Bakr went in first to make sure it was safe."
msgstr "Suka isa wani kogo a Dutsen Thawr. Abu Bakr ya shiga da farko don ya tabbatar yana da aminci."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought his milking sheep to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. At dawn he drove the flock along ‘Abdullah’s trail, and the sheep wiped out his footprints."
msgstr "Da dare ya yi, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, wanda Abu Bakr ya ’yanta, ya kawo tumakinsa masu nono zuwa kogon, don su biyun su sami sabon madara. Da asuba, ya bi hanyar ‘Abdullah yana kiwon garken, tumakin kuma suka goge sawun ƙafafunsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Amir brought sheep every evening for milk. In the morning, the sheep walked over ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "‘Amir ya kan kawo tumaki kowace maraice don a sami madara. Da safe, tumakin sukan bi ta kan sawun ƙafafun ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Searchers stood right above the cave! Abu Bakr was afraid they would look down. The Prophet ﷺ calmed his friend."
msgstr "Masu bincike sun tsaya daidai saman kogon! Abu Bakr ya ji tsoron za su leƙa ƙasa. Annabi ﷺ ya kwantar wa abokinsa hankali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the guide came with the camels, as arranged, and now there were four of them, with ‘Amir riding behind Abu Bakr. The guide led them down below Makkah and out along the coast, “by the edge of the sea.”"
msgstr "Sai jagoran ya zo da raƙuma, kamar yadda aka shirya, kuma yanzu sun zama huɗu, ‘Amir yana hawa a bayan Abu Bakr. Jagoran ya bi da su ta ƙasan Makkah zuwa bakin teku, “gefen teku.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After three nights, their guide came with the camels, and they rode out along the coast by the sea."
msgstr "Bayan dare uku, jagoransu ya zo da raƙuma, suka hau suka bi bakin teku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People on the road knew Abu Bakr, but not the man with him. “Who is this man in front of you?” they asked. “This man guides me on the way,” he answered. They thought he meant the road; he meant the way of good."
msgstr "Mutanen da ke kan hanya sun san Abu Bakr, amma ba su san mutumin da yake tare da shi ba. “Wane ne wannan mutumin da ke tare da kai?” suka tambaya. “Yana jagorance ni a hanya,” ya amsa. Suka ɗauka yana nufin hanyar tafiya; amma yana nufin hanyar alheri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People asked Abu Bakr who was with him. “He guides me on the way,” he said: the way of good."
msgstr "Mutane suka tambayi Abu Bakr ko wanene wanda yake tare da shi. “Yana jagorance ni a hanya,” ya ce, yana nufin hanyar alheri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh had put a price on the two. A man told Suraqah ibn Malik he had seen dark figures by the coast. “I knew that it was them,” Suraqah said, but he told the man otherwise. He wanted the hundred camels for himself."
msgstr "Quraysh ta sa tukuicin kama su biyun. Wani mutum ya gaya wa Suraqah ibn Malik cewa ya ga wasu siffofi masu duhu a bakin teku. “Na san su ne,” in ji Suraqah, amma ya gaya wa mutumin wani abu dabam. Yana son ya karɓi raƙuma ɗari shi kaɗai."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the road by the sea, a rider called Suraqah raced after them on his horse, hoping for a big reward."
msgstr "A hanyar bakin teku, wani mahayi mai suna Suraqah ya bi su da gudu a kan dokinsa, yana fatan samun tukuici mai yawa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode hard until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ did not look back; Abu Bakr kept looking back. Then his horse’s forelegs sank into the ground up to the knees, and Suraqah fell."
msgstr "Ya yi ta gudu har ya ji Annabi ﷺ yana karatu. Annabi ﷺ bai waiwaya ba; Abu Bakr kuwa yana ta waiwaya. Sai ƙafafun gaban dokinsa suka nutse cikin ƙasa har gwiwoyi, Suraqah kuma ya faɗi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah called out for safety and offered them provisions. They asked only, “Keep our whereabouts hidden.” ‘Amir wrote him a letter of safety on leather, and Suraqah rode back, turning every pursuer home."
msgstr "Suraqah ya nemi a ba shi kariya, ya kuma miƙa musu guzuri. Abin da suka roƙa kawai shi ne, “Ka ɓoye inda muke.” ‘Amir ya rubuta masa takardar zaman lafiya a kan fata, Suraqah kuma ya koma da dokinsa, yana mai tura duk masu binsu su koma gida."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah gave up the chase. They asked him only to keep their secret, and he sent the other riders home."
msgstr "Suraqah ya daina bin su. Abin da suka roƙa kawai shi ne ya ɓoye sirrinsu, sai ya tura sauran mahayan dawaki gida."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They rode on, but their food had run out in a year of drought. By the road stood the two tents of Umm Ma‘bad, a woman who gave water and food to those who passed. They asked to buy meat and dates, but she had none."
msgstr "Suka ci gaba da tafiya, amma guzurinsu ya ƙare a shekarar fari. A bakin hanya akwai tanti biyu na Umm Ma‘bad, matar da ke ba wa matafiya ruwa da abinci. Suka nemi su sayi nama da dabino, amma ba ta da su."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hungry and far from home, they stopped at the tent of Umm Ma‘bad. She had no food to give them."
msgstr "Suna jin yunwa kuma sun yi nisa da gida, sai suka tsaya a tantin Umm Ma‘bad. Ba ta da abincin da za ta ba su."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the back of her tent stood a ewe too weak to follow the flock. The Prophet ﷺ passed his hand over her udder, spoke the name of Allah, and milked until froth rose over the vessel. Umm Ma‘bad drank first, he drank last."
msgstr "A bayan tantinta akwai tunkiya da ta yi rauni sosai har ba ta iya bin garken. Annabi ﷺ ya shafi nononta da hannunsa, ya ambaci sunan Allah, ya kuma tatso madarar har kumfa ta cika bakin mazubin. Umm Ma‘bad ta sha da farko, shi kuma ya sha a ƙarshe."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Her thin sheep had no milk. The Prophet ﷺ said Allah’s name and milked her, and everyone drank!"
msgstr "Ƙaramar tunkiyarta ba ta da madara. Annabi ﷺ ya ambaci sunan Allah ya tatso ta, sai kowa ya sha!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she described their guest: a man of shining beauty, his words like beads slipping from a string. “By Allah,” said Abu Ma‘bad, “that is the man from Quraysh.”"
msgstr "Da mijinta ya dawo gida, ta kwatanta musu baƙonsu: mutum mai kyakkyawar fuska mai annuri, kalamansa kamar ƙwayoyin ado da ke zamewa daga zare. “Na rantse da Allah,” in ji Abu Ma‘bad, “shi ne mutumin Quraysh.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she told him about their guest: a shining face, and words like beads on a string."
msgstr "Da mijinta ya dawo gida, ta ba shi labarin baƙonsu: fuskarsa tana da annuri, kalamansa kuma kamar ƙwayoyin ado a zare."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each morning the Muslims of Madinah watched for him till the heat drove them in. Then a man on a fort saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is your good fortune, the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Kowace safiya Musulman Madinah suna sa ido su gan shi har zafin rana ya sa su koma ciki. Sai wani mutum da ke kan hasumiya ya hangi matafiyan sanye da fararen kaya, suna kyalli a cikin zirin iska: “Ga farin cikinku, ga wanda kuke jira!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Madinah, people waited every morning in the hot sun. At last a man shouted: he is here!"
msgstr "A Madinah, mutane suna jira kowace safiya a ƙarƙashin zafin rana. A ƙarshe wani mutum ya yi ihu: “Ga shi nan!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him at Quba, in the shade of a palm with Abu Bakr. Most had never seen him, and they greeted Abu Bakr. Then the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr held his cloak over him, and at that they knew him."
msgstr "Suka same shi a Quba, a inuwar dabino tare da Abu Bakr. Yawancinsu ba su taɓa ganinsa ba, saboda haka suka gaishe da Abu Bakr. Sai hasken rana ya faɗa kan Annabi ﷺ, Abu Bakr ya ɗaga mayafinsa ya yi masa inuwa, a lokacin ne suka gane shi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him resting in the shade of a palm tree at Quba, with Abu Bakr beside him."
msgstr "Suka same shi yana hutawa a inuwar dabino a Quba, Abu Bakr na gefensa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There ‘Ali caught up with him, after three days in Makkah returning what people had left in the Prophet’s ﷺ care. The Prophet ﷺ founded his mosque at Quba and prayed in it, and on a Friday he rode on towards Madinah."
msgstr "A nan ne ‘Ali ya same shi, bayan ya kwashe kwana uku a Makkah yana mayar wa mutane kayansu da suka damƙa wa Annabi ﷺ. Annabi ﷺ ya kafa masallacinsa a Quba kuma ya yi salla a cikinsa. A ranar Juma’a, ya hau ya kama hanyar Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At Quba he built a mosque and prayed in it. Then he rode on into Madinah."
msgstr "A Quba ya gina masallaci kuma ya yi salla a cikinsa. Sai ya hau ya ci gaba da tafiya zuwa Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the way he prayed his first Friday prayer in Madinah. Clan after clan came out: “Stay with us. We have the numbers and the strength.” Each time he said of his camel, “Let her go her way; she is under orders.”"
msgstr "A hanya ya yi sallar Juma’a ta farko a Madinah. Dangi-dangi suka fito suna cewa: “Ka zauna tare da mu. Muna da jama’a da ƙarfi.” A kowane lokaci sai ya ce game da raƙumarsa: “Ku bar ta ta bi hanyarta; an umurce ta.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last the Prophet ﷺ rode into Madinah. Family after family asked him to stay, but he let his camel walk on."
msgstr "A ƙarshe Annabi ﷺ ya hau raƙumarsa ya shiga Madinah. Iyali-iyali suka roƙe shi ya zauna tare da su, amma ya bar raƙumarsa ta ci gaba."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The whole town poured out, and women on the rooftops strained to see: “Which one is he?” At last the camel knelt in a yard where dates were laid to dry. “This, if Allah wills, is the stopping place,” he said."
msgstr "Dukan mutanen garin suka fito, mata kuma suka leƙa daga saman gidaje don su gani: “Wanne ne shi?” A ƙarshe raƙumar ta durƙusa a wani fili da ake shimfiɗa dabino don busarwa. “Wannan ne wurin zama, in Allah ya so,” ya ce."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Children ran and people climbed up high to see him. His camel knelt in a yard where dates were dried."
msgstr "Yara suka ruga, mutane kuma suka hau wurare masu tsawo don su gan shi. Raƙumarsa ta durƙusa a wani fili da ake busar da dabino."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There his mosque rose, from bricks of sun-dried clay. The Prophet ﷺ carried them with the others, chanting, “O Allah, there is no good but the good of the Hereafter, so help the Ansar and the Emigrants.”"
msgstr "A nan ne masallacinsa ya tashi, da tubalan laka da aka busar da su da rana. Annabi ﷺ ya riƙa ɗaukar tubalan tare da sauran mutane, yana rera waƙa: “Ya Allah, babu alheri sai alherin Lahira, saboda haka Ka taimaki Ansar da Muhajirun.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There they built a mosque, and the Prophet ﷺ carried bricks to help."
msgstr "A nan suka gina masallaci, Annabi ﷺ kuma ya taimaka ta wurin ɗaukar tubali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the fever of Madinah laid his companions low. Makkah had been the dearest of lands to him, and now he prayed for their new home: “O Allah, make Madinah dear to us as You made Makkah dear to us, or dearer.”"
msgstr "Daga nan zazzabin Madinah ya kwantar da sahabbansa. Makkah ce ƙasar da ta fi soyuwa a gare shi, amma yanzu ya yi addu’a game da sabon gidansu: “Ya Allah, Ka sanya Madinah ta soyu a gare mu kamar yadda Ka sanya Makkah ta soyu a gare mu, ko ma fiye da haka.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He prayed that Allah would make Madinah as dear to them as Makkah, and even dearer."
msgstr "Ya roƙi Allah Ya sanya Madinah ta soyu a gare su kamar Makkah, ko ma fiye da haka."

