#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari, Sahih al-Bukhari, 5/66"
msgstr "Al-Bukhari, Sahih al-Bukhari, 5/66"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Muslim, Sahih Muslim, 2/1003"
msgstr "Muslim, Sahih Muslim, 2/1003"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bayhaqi, Dala'il al-Nubuwwah, 2/518"
msgstr "Al-Bayhaqi, Dala'il al-Nubuwwah, 2/518"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers came close, so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Masu neman su sun matso kusa, har Abu Bakr ya raɗa da cewa, “Da ɗayansu ya kalli ƙafafunsa, da ya gan mu.” Annabi ﷺ ya amsa, “Me kake tunani game da mutum biyu, alhali Allah ne na uku tare da su?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Nor were they alone. Each night Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah came after dark with whatever Quraysh were plotting, then slipped back before dawn, so that morning found him in Makkah as if he had never left."
msgstr "Ba su kaɗai ba ne kuma. Kowace dare, ‘Abdullah ɗan Abu Bakr yana zuwa bayan dare ya yi da duk labarin abin da Quraysh suke ƙullawa, sannan ya koma a ɓoye kafin wayewar gari, har gari ya waye ya same shi a Makkah kamar bai taɓa barin wurin ba."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A home had to be offered before anyone could leave: the pledges at al-‘Aqabah gave the believers somewhere to go."
msgstr "Dole ne a samar da wurin zama kafin kowa ya iya barin gida: alƙawuran da aka ɗauka a al-‘Aqabah sun ba muminai wurin zuwa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Waiting on Allah’s permission and preparing every detail went together: camels fed for months, a guide hired, food packed."
msgstr "Jiran izinin Allah ya tafi tare da shirya komai: an ciyar da raƙuma na tsawon watanni, aka ɗauki jagora, aka shirya abinci."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "His honesty held even then: on the night Quraysh plotted his death, he left ‘Ali to return all that Makkah had entrusted to him."
msgstr "Amana tasa ta tabbata har a lokacin: a daren da Quraysh suka ƙulla makircin kashe shi, ya bar ‘Ali domin ya mayar da duk abin da mutanen Makkah suka ba shi ajiya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the most frightening moment came the calmest words: “Do not grieve; Allah is with us.”"
msgstr "A lokacin da ya fi firgitarwa ne aka furta kalmomi mafi kwantar da hankali: “Kada ka yi baƙin ciki; Allah yana tare da mu.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hunted as they were, they kept to the truth: “This man guides me on the way,” Abu Bakr said, and meant the way of good."
msgstr "Ko da ana farautarsu, sun tsaya kan gaskiya: “Wannan mutumin yana shiryar da ni a hanya,” in ji Abu Bakr, yana nufin hanyar alheri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hearts can turn in a moment: the man who rode out to capture them rode back to send every pursuer home."
msgstr "Zukata kan sauya nan take: mutumin da ya fita da dokinsa domin kama su ya koma yana aika duk masu binsu gida."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Blessing came to a tent with nothing to give, and the Prophet ﷺ, who brought it, drank last of all."
msgstr "Albarka ta zo wa wata tantani da ba ta da abin bayarwa, kuma Annabi ﷺ, wanda ya kawo ta, shi ne ya sha a ƙarshe."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At Quba the Prophet ﷺ founded the first mosque where he prayed openly with his companions, a mosque built on God-consciousness."
msgstr "A Quba ne Annabi ﷺ ya kafa masallaci na farko inda ya yi salla a fili tare da sahabbansa, masallacin da aka gina bisa taƙawa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah became home by being built together: emigrants and Ansar raised the mosque side by side, and were made brothers."
msgstr "Madinah ta zama gida ta hanyar gina ta tare: Muhajirai da Ansar suka gina masallaci kafada da kafada, kuma aka mai da su ‘yan’uwa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "You followed the Hijrah from a promise made by night at al-‘Aqabah to a prayer for Madinah: a long wait, three nights in a cave, a hunter turned protector, and a whole town out to welcome him."
msgstr "Ka bi labarin Hijrah tun daga alƙawarin da aka ɗauka da dare a al-‘Aqabah har zuwa addu’ar Madinah: dogon jira, dare uku a cikin kogo, mafarauci da ya zama mai kāre su, da kuma dukkan gari da ya fito tarbarsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "His home, where he waited for permission and from where he slipped out by night with Abu Bakr."
msgstr "Gidansa, inda ya jira izini kuma ya fice da dare tare da Abu Bakr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr hid in a cave for three nights while Quraysh searched for them."
msgstr "Wurin da Annabi ﷺ da Abu Bakr suka ɓuya a cikin kogo na dare uku yayin da Quraysh ke nemansu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide led them down to the sea and along the shore, station after station, towards Madinah."
msgstr "Jagoran ya kai su zuwa bakin teku, suka bi gaɓar teku, suna tsayawa a wurare daban-daban, zuwa Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where Madinah’s Muslims first met him, under a palm, and where he founded his mosque."
msgstr "Wurin da Musulman Madinah suka fara haɗuwa da shi, a ƙarƙashin bishiyar dabino, kuma inda ya kafa masallacinsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where his camel knelt, his mosque rose, and the emigrants made a new home."
msgstr "Wurin da raƙumarsa ta durƙusa, aka gina masallacinsa, kuma Muhajirai suka kafa sabon gida."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Under Abu Ayyub’s roof"
msgstr "A ƙarƙashin rufin Abu Ayyub"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Ayyub carried the Prophet’s ﷺ saddle into his house. One day a jar of water broke upstairs, and he and his wife soaked it up with their only blanket, so that not a drop would fall on their guest."
msgstr "Abu Ayyub ya ɗauki sirdin Annabi ﷺ zuwa cikin gidansa. Wata rana tulun ruwa ya fashe a bene na sama, sai shi da matarsa suka tsotse ruwan da bargonsu tilo, don kada ko digo ɗaya ya zubo kan baƙonsu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When water spilled upstairs, Abu Ayyub and his wife mopped it up with their only blanket, so none dripped on him."
msgstr "Da ruwa ya zubo a bene na sama, Abu Ayyub da matarsa suka share shi da bargonsu tilo, don kada ya ɗiga a kansa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "She of the two waistbands"
msgstr "Mai ɗamara biyu"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In another telling, it was at the cave that Asma’s waistband served them. She had brought their food but forgotten a strap to hang it by, so she split her waistband in two and hung the bag with one half."
msgstr "A wani ruwaya kuma, ɗamarar Asma ce ta taimake su a kogon. Ta kawo musu abinci amma ta manta da igiyar rataya shi, sai ta tsaga ɗamararta gida biyu ta rataya jakar da ɗaya rabin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma had nothing to tie up their food bag, so she split her waistband in two and used one half."
msgstr "Asma ba ta da abin ɗaure jakar abincinsu, sai ta tsaga ɗamararta gida biyu ta yi amfani da ɗaya rabin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ made each emigrant a brother to one of the Ansar who had taken them in. Each pair stood by the other and shared what they had, and at first such brothers even inherited from one another."
msgstr "Annabi ﷺ ya ɗaura kowane Muhajiri da wani daga cikin Ansar da suka karɓe su a matsayin ‘yan’uwa. Kowanne ma’aurata ya taimaki ɗan’uwansa kuma suka raba abin da suke da shi; da farko ma, irin waɗannan ‘yan’uwa suna gadon juna."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He made each newcomer a brother to someone from Madinah, so they would help each other and share."
msgstr "Ya ɗaura kowane sabon zuwa da wani daga Madinah a matsayin ‘yan’uwa, domin su taimaki juna kuma su raba abin da suke da shi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Let her go her way"
msgstr "A bar ta ta ci gaba da tafiyarta"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Even his mother’s kin, Banu ‘Adi ibn al-Najjar, called out, “Come to your mother’s people.” “Let her go her way,” he said. “She is under orders.” She walked on, and knelt among Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Har dangin mahaifiyarsa, Banu ‘Adi ibn al-Najjar, suka kira shi: “Zo wurin mutanen mahaifiyarka.” Ya ce: “A bar ta ta ci gaba da tafiyarta. An umurce ta.” Ta ci gaba da tafiya, ta kuma durƙusa a tsakanin Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Everyone wanted the Prophet ﷺ to stay with them. “Let my camel go,” he said. “She knows where to stop.”"
msgstr "Kowa yana son Annabi ﷺ ya sauka a wurinsa. “Ku bar rakumina ta tafi,” ya ce. “Ta san inda za ta tsaya.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode out of Quba on a Friday. On the way, the time for prayer came among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, and he prayed it in their mosque in the valley of Ranuna: his first Friday prayer in Madinah."
msgstr "Ya fito daga Quba a ranar Juma’a. A hanya, lokacin sallah ya yi a wajen Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, sai ya yi ta a masallacinsu da ke kwarin Ranuna. Wannan ita ce sallar Juma’arsa ta farko a Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On his way into Madinah, the Prophet ﷺ stopped to lead the Friday prayer for the very first time there."
msgstr "A kan hanyarsa ta shiga Madinah, Annabi ﷺ ya tsaya ya jagoranci sallar Juma’a a karon farko a can."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Dressed in white"
msgstr "Sanye da fararen kaya"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the road they met al-Zubayr, coming home from Syria with Muslim merchants, and he dressed the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr in white. It was in white, shimmering in the mirage, that they were first seen from Madinah."
msgstr "A hanya suka haɗu da al-Zubayr, wanda yake dawowa daga Sham tare da ’yan kasuwa Musulmi. Ya ba Annabi ﷺ da Abu Bakr fararen kaya. Daga Madinah aka fara hango su sanye da fararen kaya, suna kyalli a cikin zafin iska."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the way, their friend al-Zubayr gave them white clothes to wear."
msgstr "A hanya, abokinsu al-Zubayr ya ba su fararen kaya su saka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As he came, the women and children of Madinah sang: “The full moon has risen over us, from the passes of al-Wada‘. Thanks are due from us, as long as anyone calls to Allah.”"
msgstr "Yayin da yake zuwa, matan Madinah da yara suka rera waka: “Cikakken wata ya fito a kanmu, daga mashigar al-Wada‘. Godiya ta tabbata a gare mu, matuƙar akwai mai kiran mutane zuwa ga Allah.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The women and children sang a song of welcome: “The full moon has risen over us!”"
msgstr "Matan Madinah da yara suka rera waƙar maraba: “Cikakken wata ya fito a kanmu!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "South, not north"
msgstr "Kudu, ba arewa ba"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah lay to the north, but that was not the road they took. Under cover of night they turned the opposite way, south on the road towards Yemen, and went about five miles to Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah tana arewa, amma ba wannan hanyar suka bi ba. Da dare suka juya akasin haka, suka nufi kudu a hanyar Yemen, suka yi tafiyar kusan mil biyar zuwa Dutsen Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah was to the north, but they went south first, to a mountain called Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah tana arewa, amma da farko suka nufi kudu, zuwa wani dutse mai suna Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The road by the sea"
msgstr "Hanyar bakin teku"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide led them down below Makkah and along the coast, out onto the road below ‘Usfan. Then he took them by lower Amaj, and back to the road past Qudayd, one station after another."
msgstr "Mai shiryarwar ya bi da su ta kudancin Makkah, ya bi bakin teku har zuwa hanyar da ke ƙasan ‘Usfan. Daga nan ya bi da su ta ƙasan Amaj, ya koma hanyar da ta wuce Qudayd, daga wannan masauki zuwa wancan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their guide knew the desert well. He led them down to the sea and along the coast, from one place to the next."
msgstr "Mai shiryarwarsu ya san hamada sosai. Ya bi da su zuwa bakin teku, suka bi gabar teku daga wani wuri zuwa wani."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In the full heat of noon, someone called to Abu Bakr: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at the door, his head covered, at an hour he never came. “Allah has given me permission to leave,” he said."
msgstr "A tsakiyar zafin rana, wani ya sanar da Abu Bakr cewa Manzon Allah ﷺ yana bakin ƙofa, kansa a rufe. Ba ya zuwa a irin wannan lokaci. “Allah Ya ba ni izinin tafiya,” ya ce."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One hot noon the Prophet ﷺ knocked at Abu Bakr’s door with big news: “Allah has given me permission to leave.”"
msgstr "A wani zafin rana, Annabi ﷺ ya ƙwanƙwasa ƙofar Abu Bakr da babban labari: “Allah Ya ba ni izinin tafiya.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "All his money"
msgstr "Dukan kuɗinsa"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When Abu Bakr slipped out with the Prophet ﷺ that night, by a small door at the back of his house, he carried all his money with him: five or six thousand dirhams."
msgstr "Da Abu Bakr ya sulale da Annabi ﷺ a daren, ta wata ƙaramar ƙofa a bayan gidansa, ya tafi da dukan kuɗinsa: dirhami dubu biyar ko shida."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money with him for the journey, thousands of silver coins."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ya tafi da dukan kuɗinsa a wannan tafiya, dubban tsabar azurfa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the mountain the trail grew confused, so the searchers climbed it and passed by the cave. Seeing a spider’s web across its entrance, they said, “If anyone had gone in here, there would be no web over it.”"
msgstr "A dutsen, sawun ya rikice, sai masu nemansu suka hau dutsen suka wuce ta kogon. Da suka ga gizo-gizo ya yi saƙar yanar gizo a bakin kogon, sai suka ce: “Da wani ya shiga nan, da babu wannan saƙar a bakin kogon.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers saw a spider’s web across the cave’s opening. “No one went in there,” they said, and walked on."
msgstr "Masu nemansu suka ga saƙar gizo-gizo a bakin kogon. “Ba wanda ya shiga nan,” suka ce, suka wuce."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah gives three nights. Which nights of the week they were was worked out by later biographers."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta ce dare uku ne. Marubutan tarihin rayuwa na baya ne suka ƙayyade ranakun makon da waɗannan darare suka faɗa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Into Madinah, on a Friday"
msgstr "Shiga Madinah a ranar Juma’a"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Friday, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"
msgstr "Juma’a, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 Satumba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq gives the Friday he left Quba; the day of the month was worked out by a modern biographer."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya ambaci ranar Juma’a da ya bar Quba; wani marubucin tarihin rayuwa na zamani ne ya ƙayyade ranar watan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide comes with the camels"
msgstr "Jagoran ya zo tare da raƙuman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Night of 1 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 16 September 622"
msgstr "Daren 1 ga Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 16 ga Satumba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came after the third night, as agreed. Later biographers date it to the night of Monday."
msgstr "Ya zo bayan dare na uku, kamar yadda aka yi yarjejeniya. Marubutan tarihin da suka zo daga baya sun ce daren Litinin ne."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He had stayed on in Makkah through Muharram and Safar. The exact night was worked out by a modern biographer."
msgstr "Ya ci gaba da zama a Makkah a cikin watannin Muharram da Safar. Wani marubucin tarihin zamani ne ya ƙiyasta ainihin daren."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A Monday in Rabi‘ al-Awwal · September 622"
msgstr "Wata Litinin a Rabi‘ al-Awwal · Satumba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The reports agree it was a Monday. Ibn Ishaq gives the twelfth of the month; others give other days."
msgstr "Riwayoyin sun yarda cewa Litinin ce. Ibn Ishaq ya ce rana ta goma sha biyu ga watan ce; wasu kuma sun ambaci wasu ranaku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah on their trail"
msgstr "Suraqah yana bin sawunsu"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A Tuesday, after the noon rest at Qudayd"
msgstr "Wata Talata, bayan hutun azahar a Qudayd"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Sa‘d gives this day; the other reports tell what happened in order, but name no day."
msgstr "Ibn Sa‘d ya ambaci wannan rana; sauran riwayoyin sun ba da labarin abubuwan da suka faru a jere, amma ba su ambaci rana ba."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "From four days to fourteen nights"
msgstr "Daga kwana huɗu zuwa dare goma sha huɗu"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq counts Monday to Thursday; ‘Urwah speaks of ten nights and more, and Anas of fourteen."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya ƙirga daga Litinin zuwa Alhamis; ‘Urwah ya ce dare goma ko fiye, Anas kuma ya ce goma sha huɗu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how many went ahead to Madinah, while Abu Bakr held himself back to travel with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta ba da labarin waɗanda suka riga su zuwa Madinah, yayin da Abu Bakr ya dakata domin ya yi tafiya tare da Annabi ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah recalls the family making them ready in haste, and Asma tying the food bag with a piece of her waistband."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta tuna yadda iyalin suka yi musu tanadi cikin gaggawa, da yadda Asma ta ɗaure jakar abinci da wani yanki na ɗamarar rigarta."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how her brother ‘Abdullah spent the nights with them, was among Quraysh by morning, and brought their news after dark."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta ba da labarin yadda ɗan’uwanta ‘Abdullah yake kwana tare da su, ya kasance cikin mutanen Quraysh da safe, sannan ya kawo musu labaransu bayan duhu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought his milking sheep to the cave after nightfall, on each of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta ba da labarin yadda ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah yake kawo tumakinsa mai nono zuwa kogon bayan dare ya yi, a kowane dare daga cikin ukun."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how they hired a skilled guide of Banu al-Dil, gave him their two camels, and set the meeting at Thawr."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta ba da labarin yadda suka ɗauki ƙwararren jagora daga Banu al-Dil aiki, suka ba shi raƙumansu biyu, suka kuma sanya Thawr a matsayin wurin haɗuwa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah and the guide set out with them, and how the guide took them by the coast road."
msgstr "‘Aishah ta ba da labarin yadda ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah da jagoran suka tashi tare da su, da yadda jagoran ya bi da su ta hanyar bakin teku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how Madinah heard he had left Makkah, and how he stayed among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf for ten nights and more."
msgstr "‘Urwah ya ba da labarin yadda Madinah ta sami labarin cewa ya bar Makkah, da yadda ya zauna a tsakanin Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf na dare goma ko fiye."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how the yard was built into a mosque, with the Prophet ﷺ carrying bricks alongside the builders."
msgstr "‘Urwah ya ba da labarin yadda aka gina masallaci a filin, Annabi ﷺ kuma yana ɗaukar tubalin tare da masu ginin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah recalls the blood-money offered for each of the two, and a man who had just seen dark figures by the coast."
msgstr "Suraqah ya tuna da ladan diyya da aka yi alkawarin bayarwa ga duk wanda ya kama ɗayansu, da kuma mutumin da ya ga wasu siffofi masu duhu kusa da bakin teku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah describes hearing the Prophet ﷺ recite, Abu Bakr looking back, and his own horse sinking to its knees."
msgstr "Suraqah ya kwatanta yadda ya ji Annabi ﷺ yana karatu, Abu Bakr yana waiwaya, da yadda dokinsa ya nutse har gwiwoyinsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah recalls that they took nothing he offered and asked only for secrecy, and that ‘Amir wrote him a letter of safety on leather."
msgstr "Suraqah ya tuna cewa ba su karɓi komai daga abin da ya miƙa ba, sun roƙe shi kawai ya ɓoye batunsu, kuma ‘Amir ya rubuta masa takardar kariya a kan fata."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how he stayed among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf, founded the mosque built on God-consciousness, and prayed in it."
msgstr "‘Urwah ya ba da labarin yadda ya zauna a tsakanin Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf, ya kafa masallacin da aka gina bisa tsoron Allah, kuma ya yi sallah a cikinsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how people walked beside his camel until she knelt where his mosque now stands, then a yard for drying dates."
msgstr "‘Urwah ya ba da labarin yadda mutane suka yi tafiya a gefen raƙumarsa har sai da ta durƙusa a wurin da masallacinsa yake a yau, wanda a lokacin filin busar da dabino ne."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how Quraysh, now afraid of him, met in Dar al-Nadwah, the house where they settled all their affairs."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya ba da labarin yadda Quraysh, da suka fara jin tsoronsa, suka haɗu a Dar al-Nadwah, gidan da suke yanke shawara kan dukkan al’amuransu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Seeing the men at his door, the Prophet ﷺ tells ‘Ali to sleep in his bed under his green cloak, and promises him safety."
msgstr "Da ya ga mutanen a ƙofarsa, Annabi ﷺ ya gaya wa ‘Ali ya kwanta a shimfiɗarsa ƙarƙashin mayafinsa kore, ya kuma yi masa alƙawarin tsira."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells why ‘Ali stayed behind: anyone in Makkah who feared for something precious had left it with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya bayyana dalilin da ya sa ‘Ali ya tsaya a baya: duk wanda ke Makkah yake tsoron kada wani abu mai daraja ya ɓace, ya bar shi a hannun Annabi ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Ibn Ishaq’s telling she has no food and only dry ewes; he milks one until the bowl froths: “Drink, Umm Ma‘bad.”"
msgstr "A riwayar Ibn Ishaq, ba ta da abinci, kuma tumakinta mata busassu ne kawai. Ya shayar da ɗaya daga cikinsu har madarar ta cika kwano da kumfa, ya ce: “Ki sha, Umm Ma‘bad.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah remembers the noon visit, and Abu Bakr asking at once to go with him: “Companionship?” “Yes.”"
msgstr "‘Aishah ta tuna ziyarar da aka yi da tsakar rana, da Abu Bakr ya roƙi nan take ya tafi tare da shi: “Zan raka ka?” “Eh.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma recalls her father taking all his money, and the stones she laid where it had been kept, under a cloth, to calm her grandfather."
msgstr "Asma ta tuna mahaifinta ya ɗauki duk kuɗinsa, da duwatsun da ta sa a wurin da aka ajiye kuɗin, ta rufe su da zane don kwantar wa kakanta hankali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri notes that he took the very opposite road from the one expected, south of Makkah towards Yemen."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri ya lura cewa ya bi hanyar da ta saɓa wa wadda ake tsammani, ya nufi kudu da Makkah, zuwa Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq places Asma’s waistband at the cave, and gives it as the reason she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya ce Asma ta yi amfani da ɗamararta a kogon, kuma wannan ne dalilin da ya sa aka kira ta Dhat al-Nitaqayn."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn ‘Abbas tells of the web across the cave’s mouth; Ibn Kathir counts this among the best reports of it."
msgstr "Ibn ‘Abbas ya ba da labarin gizo-gizon da ya rufe bakin kogon; Ibn Kathir ya ɗauki wannan a matsayin ɗaya daga cikin ingantattun riwayoyin labarin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq names the places on the guide’s route, one by one, from below Makkah to the road beyond Qudayd."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya ambaci wuraren da jagoran ya bi, ɗaya bayan ɗaya, daga kudancin Makkah zuwa hanyar da ta wuce Qudayd."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells of the meeting with al-Zubayr’s caravan of Muslim merchants, and the white clothes he gave the two travellers."
msgstr "‘Urwah ya ba da labarin haɗuwarsu da ayarin ‘yan kasuwar Musulmi na al-Zubayr, da fararen tufafin da ya ba matafiyan biyu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri tells of the first Friday prayer among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, with a hundred men, in the mosque in the valley."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri ya ba da labarin sallar Juma’a ta farko a cikin Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, inda mutum ɗari suka yi salla a masallacin da ke kwarin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how each clan was answered, “Let her go, for she is under orders,” until she knelt among Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya ba da labarin yadda aka amsa wa kowace ƙabila da cewa, “Ku sake ta, umarni ne aka ba ta,” har sai da ta durƙusa a cikin Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how he lodged with Abu Ayyub until his mosque and rooms were built, working on them with emigrants and Ansar."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya ba da labarin yadda ya sauka a gidan Abu Ayyub har aka gina masallacinsa da ɗakunansa, tare da taimakon Muhajirai da Ansar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir’s heading for the brotherhood: the Prophet ﷺ paired emigrants with Ansar so each newcomer had someone to lean on."
msgstr "Taken Ibn Kathir game da ‘yan’uwantaka: Annabi ﷺ ya haɗa Muhajirai da Ansar biyu-biyu, don kowane sabon zuwa ya samu wanda zai dogara gare shi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn ‘A'ishah, a later narrator who does not say who told him, describes women and children singing as the Prophet ﷺ arrived."
msgstr "Ibn ‘A'ishah, wani mai ba da labari na baya wanda bai faɗi wanda ya ba shi labarin ba, ya bayyana yadda mata da yara suka rera waƙa sa’ad da Annabi ﷺ ya iso."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates the night he left his house: 27 Safar, in the fourteenth year of his prophethood."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri ya bayyana cewa daren da ya bar gidansa shi ne 27 ga Safar, a shekara ta goma sha huɗu ta annabcinsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri names the three nights in the cave: the nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri ya ambaci darare ukun da aka yi a kogon: dararen da suka gabaci Juma’a, Asabar da Lahadi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates the guide’s coming with the two camels to the night of Monday, the first of Rabi‘ al-Awwal."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri ya ce jagoran ya zo da raƙuma biyu a daren Litinin, 1 ga Rabi‘ al-Awwal."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah gives the day he came down among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf: a Monday in the month of Rabi‘ al-Awwal."
msgstr "‘Urwah ya bayyana ranar da ya sauka a cikin Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf: Litinin a watan Rabi‘ al-Awwal."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir sets Ibn Ishaq’s four days, Monday to Thursday, beside ‘Urwah’s report of ten nights and more."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir ya kwatanta kwanaki huɗu na Ibn Ishaq, daga Litinin zuwa Alhamis, da riwayar ‘Urwah ta darare goma ko fiye."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates his arrival among Banu al-Najjar to Friday, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal, in the first year of the Hijrah."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri ya ce ya isa wurin Banu al-Najjar a ranar Juma’a, 12 ga Rabi‘ al-Awwal, a shekara ta farko bayan Hijira."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir gives her name, ‘Atikah, and her family, and calls her story well known, through routes that support one another."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir ya ambaci sunanta, ‘Atikah, da danginta, ya kuma ce labarinta sananne ne, ta hanyoyin riwaya da ke ƙarfafa juna."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Stones under a cloth"
msgstr "Duwaye a ƙarƙashin wani yadi"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money, five or six thousand dirhams. When his blind father came, fearing it gone, Asma laid stones in its niche under a cloth and let him feel them."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ya ɗauki duk kuɗinsa, dirhami dubu biyar ko shida. Da mahaifinsa makaho ya zo, yana tsoron cewa kuɗin sun ɓace, Asma ta sa duwatsu a wurin da ake ajiye su, ta rufe su da yadi, sannan ta sa shi ya taɓa su."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money. To calm her blind grandfather, Asma let him feel stones under a cloth."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ya ɗauki duk kuɗinsa. Don ta kwantar wa kakanta makaho hankali, Asma ta sa shi ya taɓa duwatsu a ƙarƙashin yadi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Monday 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · September 622"
msgstr "Litinin, 12 ga Rabi‘ al-Awwal · Satumba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s date. The reports agree on a Monday but differ on the day of the month."
msgstr "Ranar da Ibn Ishaq ya bayar. Riwayoyin sun yarda cewa Litinin ce, amma sun bambanta game da ranar watan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Friday after Quba · Rabi‘ al-Awwal 622"
msgstr "Juma’ar da ta biyo bayan Quba · Rabi‘ al-Awwal 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq has him stay at Quba from Monday to Thursday and ride on to Madinah on the Friday."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq ya ce ya zauna a Quba daga Litinin zuwa Alhamis, sannan ya hau abin hawa zuwa Madinah a ranar Juma’a."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "Verification failed. Try again."
msgstr "Tabbatarwa ta gaza. Sake gwadawa."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "Retry verification"
msgstr "Sake gwada tabbatarwa"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. ‘Ali lay in the Prophet’s ﷺ bed, wrapped in his green cloak."
msgstr "A daren nan suka jira a wajen ƙofarsa. ‘Ali ya kwanta a gadon Annabi ﷺ, sanye da alkyabbarsa kore."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s helper ‘Amir brought sheep each evening for milk. At dawn the sheep walked over ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "‘Amir, mai taimaka wa Abu Bakr, yakan kawo tumaki kowace yamma domin a sha nononsu. Da asuba, tumakin suka bi ta kan sawun ƙafafun ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Some say it was here that Abu Bakr’s daughter Asma split her waistband in two, to tie up their food bag."
msgstr "Wasu sun ce a nan ne Asma, ’yar Abu Bakr, ta yaga ɗamarar ƙugunta gida biyu domin ta ɗaure jakar abincinsu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money. To calm her blind grandfather, his daughter Asma let him feel stones under a cloth."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ya ɗauki dukan kuɗinsa. Don ta kwantar wa kakanta makaho hankali, ’yarsa Asma ta sa ya taɓa duwatsu a ƙarƙashin wani kyalle."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Friday 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"
msgstr "Juma’a 12 ga Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 ga Satumba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq has him stay at Quba Monday to Thursday and ride on the Friday; a modern biographer worked out the date."
msgstr "A cewar Ibn Ishaq, ya zauna a Quba daga Litinin zuwa Alhamis, sannan ya hau abin hawa ranar Juma’a; wani marubucin tarihin rayuwa na zamani ne ya ƙiyasta ranar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari’s report has him come on the morning of the third day; later biographers date it to the night of Monday."
msgstr "Riwayar Al-Bukhari ta ce ya iso da safiyar rana ta uku; marubutan tarihin rayuwa na baya sun sanya zuwansa a daren Litinin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Monday 8 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 23 September 622"
msgstr "Litinin 8 ga Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 23 ga Satumba 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The reports agree on a Monday. A modern biographer worked out the date; Ibn Ishaq gives the twelfth."
msgstr "Riwayoyin sun yarda cewa ranar Litinin ce. Wani marubucin tarihin rayuwa na zamani ne ya ƙiyasta ranar; Ibn Ishaq ya ce ranar goma sha biyu ce."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After the noon rest at Qudayd"
msgstr "Bayan hutun azahar a Qudayd"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Sa‘d calls it a Tuesday, by his own count of the days; the other reports name no day."
msgstr "Ibn Sa‘d ya ce ranar Talata ce, bisa yadda ya ƙirga kwanakin; sauran riwayoyin ba su ambaci takamaiman rana ba."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every pilgrimage season, as the tribes came to Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ went out to them and called them to Allah. One season, at a place called al-‘Aqabah, six men from Yathrib sat down to listen."
msgstr "A kowace kakar aikin hajji, yayin da ƙabilu suke zuwa Makkah, Annabi ﷺ yana fita zuwa gare su yana kiransu zuwa ga Allah. A wata kakar, a wani wuri mai suna al-‘Aqabah, wasu maza shida daga Yathrib suka zauna don sauraro."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every year, pilgrims came to Makkah. The Prophet ﷺ told them about Allah, and six men from Yathrib listened."
msgstr "Kowace shekara, mahajjata suna zuwa Makkah. Annabi ﷺ yana gaya musu game da Allah, kuma wasu maza shida daga Yathrib suka saurara."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At home their Jewish neighbours often warned of a prophet soon to come. “By Allah,” the six said to one another, “this is the prophet they threatened us with.” They accepted Islam and took it home."
msgstr "A gida, maƙwabtansu Yahudawa sukan yi musu gargaɗi cewa wani annabi zai zo nan ba da daɗewa ba. “Wallahi,” shida ɗin suka ce wa juna, “wannan shi ne annabin da suke yi mana barazanar zuwansa.” Suka karɓi Musulunci, suka koma gida da shi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their Jewish neighbours said a prophet was coming. “This is him!” the six men said, and they became Muslims."
msgstr "Maƙwabtansu Yahudawa sun ce wani annabi yana zuwa. “Shi ne wannan!” mazan shida suka ce, kuma suka zama Musulmi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, those who followed the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ were insulted and harmed by Quraysh, his own tribe, who ruled the town. This is the story of the Hijrah: how they found a new home, and how he made the journey there."
msgstr "A Makkah, mutanen da suka bi Annabi Muhammad ﷺ sun fuskanci cin mutunci da cutarwa daga hannun Quraysh, mutanen kabilarsa da ke mulkin garin. Wannan ita ce labarin Hijira: yadda suka sami sabon gida, da yadda ya yi tafiya zuwa wurin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, the Prophet’s ﷺ own tribe was cruel to the Muslims. This is the story of how they found a new home."
msgstr "A Makkah, mutanen kabilar Annabi ﷺ sun wulakanta Musulmi. Wannan ita ce labarin yadda suka sami sabon gida."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every pilgrimage season, as tribes from across Arabia came to Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ went out to them and called them to Allah. One season, at al-‘Aqabah, six men from Yathrib, a town to the north, sat down to listen."
msgstr "A duk lokacin aikin hajji, yayin da kabilu daga sassa daban-daban na Larabawa suke zuwa Makkah, Annabi ﷺ yakan je wurinsu ya kira su zuwa ga Allah. A wani lokaci, a al-‘Aqabah, wasu maza shida daga Yathrib, wani gari da ke arewa, suka zauna domin su saurara."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every year, visitors came to Makkah to worship. The Prophet ﷺ told them about Allah, and six men from Yathrib listened."
msgstr "Kowace shekara, baƙi sukan zo Makkah domin ibada. Annabi ﷺ yakan ba su labarin Allah, wasu maza shida daga Yathrib kuma suka saurara."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Back home, their Jewish neighbours used to say a prophet would soon come, and they would follow him against them. “By Allah,” the six said to one another, “this is that prophet.” They accepted Islam and took it home."
msgstr "Da suka koma gida, maƙwabtansu Yahudawa sukan ce nan ba da daɗewa ba wani annabi zai zo, kuma za su bi shi su yaƙe su. “Na rantse da Allah,” shida ɗin suka ce wa juna, “wannan shi ne annabin.” Suka musulunta, suka kuma kai saƙon Musulunci gida."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Back home, their Jewish neighbours said a prophet was coming. “This is him!” the six said, and they became Muslims."
msgstr "Da suka koma gida, maƙwabtansu Yahudawa suka ce wani annabi na zuwa. “Ga shi nan!” shida ɗin suka ce, suka musulunta."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each year more came from Yathrib, until seventy-three men and two women met him there by night. They pledged to protect him, if he came, as they protected their own families. “I am of you and you are of me,” he said."
msgstr "A kowace shekara, mutane da yawa daga Yathrib sukan zo, har maza saba’in da uku da mata biyu suka haɗu da shi a wurin da dare. Sun yi alƙawarin za su kāre shi idan ya zo, kamar yadda suke kāre iyalansu. “Ni naku ne, ku kuma nawa ne,” ya ce."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Later, many more came from Yathrib at night. They promised to keep him safe, the way they kept their own families safe."
msgstr "Daga baya, mutane da yawa daga Yathrib suka zo da dare. Sun yi alƙawarin kāre shi kamar yadda suke kāre iyalansu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their new home, he told his companions, would be Yathrib, soon to be called Madinah. Group by group these Emigrants slipped away, until few were left but him, his close friend Abu Bakr and his cousin ‘Ali."
msgstr "Ya gaya wa sahabbansa cewa Yathrib ne zai zama sabon gidansu, kuma nan ba da daɗewa ba za a kira garin Madinah. Waɗannan Muhajirai suka riƙa tafiya a rukuni-rukuni a ɓoye, har sai da ba wanda ya rage sosai sai shi, amininsa Abu Bakr da ɗan’uwansa ‘Ali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "So the Muslims of Makkah moved to Yathrib, the town we call Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ waited for Allah’s permission to go."
msgstr "Don haka Musulmin Makkah suka yi hijira zuwa Yathrib, garin da muke kira Madinah. Annabi ﷺ ya jira izinin Allah domin ya tafi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr asked again and again to go too. “Do not hurry,” the Prophet ﷺ told him. “Perhaps Allah will give you a companion.” Abu Bakr hoped it would be the Prophet ﷺ himself, and fed two camels for four months."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ya riƙa roƙon a ba shi damar tafiya shi ma. “Kada ka yi gaggawa,” Annabi ﷺ ya gaya masa. “Wataƙila Allah zai ba ka abokin tafiya.” Abu Bakr ya yi fatan Annabi ﷺ ne zai zama abokin tafiyarsa, kuma ya ciyar da raƙuma biyu tsawon watanni huɗu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then one noon, at an hour he never came, the Prophet ﷺ came to Abu Bakr’s house. “Allah has given me permission to leave.” “And I am to come with you?” Abu Bakr asked. “Yes.” And Abu Bakr wept for joy."
msgstr "Wata rana da tsakar rana, a lokacin da ba kasafai yake zuwa ba, Annabi ﷺ ya zo gidan Abu Bakr. “Allah ya ba ni izinin tafiya.” Abu Bakr ya tambaya, “Ni ma zan tafi tare da kai?” “I, haka ne.” Sai Abu Bakr ya yi kuka don murna."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hired a guide to bring the camels after three nights to a cave on Mount Thawr, where they would hide. Asma, Abu Bakr’s daughter, split her waistband to tie up their food, and became “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Suka ɗauki hayar jagora wanda zai kawo raƙuman bayan dare uku zuwa wani kogo a Dutsen Thawr, inda za su ɓuya. Asma, ’yar Abu Bakr, ta tsaga ɗamarar ƙugunta domin ta ɗaure abincinsu, kuma aka yi mata laƙabi da “ma’abociyar ɗamara biyu”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh feared the Prophet ﷺ would follow his companions. In their council house, their leaders agreed to kill him: a young man from every clan would strike at once, so that no one clan could be made to answer for it."
msgstr "Quraysh sun ji tsoron Annabi ﷺ zai bi sahabbansa. A zauren shawarwarinsu, shugabanninsu suka amince su kashe shi: wani saurayi daga kowace kabila zai kai masa hari a lokaci guda, don kada a ɗora wa wata kabila ita kaɗai alhakin abin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last Allah gave him permission. But the leaders of Makkah, afraid of his message, made a plan to hurt him."
msgstr "A ƙarshe Allah ya ba shi izini. Amma shugabannin Makkah, saboda tsoron saƙonsa, suka ƙulla makircin cutar da shi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. His cousin ‘Ali lay in his bed, so they would think the Prophet ﷺ was inside."
msgstr "A wannan daren, suka yi tsaye a wajen ƙofarsa suna jiransa. Ɗan’uwansa ‘Ali ya kwanta a gadonsa, don su ɗauka Annabi ﷺ yana ciki."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then he came out to them with a handful of dust, scattering it over their heads and reciting the Quran: “So We have covered them, and they do not see.” Allah took their sight from him, and he went on his way."
msgstr "Sai ya fito ta gabansu da ƙurar da ya ɗiba a hannu, yana watsata a kawunansu da karanta Alƙur’ani: “Saboda haka muka rufe su, ba sa gani.” Allah ya hana su ganinsa, sai ya kama hanyarsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ walked right out past them, throwing a handful of dust, and Allah kept them from seeing him."
msgstr "Annabi ﷺ ya wuce ta gabansu, yana watsa ƙurar da ya ɗiba a hannu, kuma Allah ya hana su ganinsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came to Abu Bakr, and the two slipped out by a small door at the back of Abu Bakr’s house, Abu Bakr carrying all his savings. Madinah lay to the north, but they turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Ya je wurin Abu Bakr, sai su biyun suka fita a ɓoye ta wata ƙaramar ƙofa a bayan gidan Abu Bakr, yana ɗauke da duk kuɗin da ya tara. Madinah tana arewa, amma suka nufi kudu, wajen Yemen."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He and his best friend, Abu Bakr, slipped away in the dark. They went south first, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Shi da babban amininsa Abu Bakr suka fice a ɓoye cikin duhu. Da farko suka nufi kudu, sabanin hanyar Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hid in a cave on Mount Thawr. Abu Bakr went in first to make sure it was safe."
msgstr "Suka ɓuya a wani kogo a Dutsen Thawr. Abu Bakr ya fara shiga don ya tabbatar wurin yana da aminci."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh sent out searchers, and they came so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” “What do you think of two,” said the Prophet ﷺ, “when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Quraysh suka aika masu neman su, kuma suka matso sosai har Abu Bakr ya raɗa, “Da ɗayansu zai duba ƙafafunsa, da ya gan mu.” Annabi ﷺ ya ce, “Me kake tsammani game da mutum biyu, alhali Allah ne na uku tare da su?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Men from Makkah searched everywhere, and stood right above the cave! Abu Bakr was afraid. The Prophet ﷺ calmed him."
msgstr "Wasu maza daga Makkah suka bincika ko’ina, har suka tsaya a saman kogon! Abu Bakr ya ji tsoro. Annabi ﷺ ya kwantar masa da hankali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As darkness settled, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, who tended Abu Bakr’s sheep, brought the flock to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. At dawn he drove it along ‘Abdullah’s trail, and the sheep wiped out ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "Da dare ya yi, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, mai kiwon tumakin Abu Bakr, ya kawo garken zuwa kogon, don su biyun su sha nono sabo. Da gari ya waye, ya tuka garken ta hanyar sawun ‘Abdullah, tumakin kuma suka goge sawun ƙafafun ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s helper ‘Amir brought sheep each evening for milk. At dawn the sheep covered up ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "‘Amir, mataimakin Abu Bakr, yakan kawo tumaki kowace yamma don su samu nono. Da gari ya waye, tumakin sukan rufe sawun ƙafafun ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh offered a hundred camels for the two. Suraqah ibn Malik, a horseman of a tribe on the coast road, heard that riders had been seen by the sea. He knew it was them, but kept quiet: he wanted the reward himself."
msgstr "Quraysh ta bayar da raƙuma ɗari domin a kama su biyun. Suraqah ibn Malik, wani mahayin doki daga wata ƙabila da ke kan hanyar bakin teku, ya ji cewa an ga wasu mahaya a kusa da teku. Ya san su ne, amma ya yi shiru: yana son ladan ya zama nasa shi kaɗai."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After three nights they rode on by the sea. A rider called Suraqah raced after them, hoping for a reward."
msgstr "Bayan kwana uku, suka ci gaba da tafiya a gefen teku. Wani mahayi mai suna Suraqah ya ruga a bayansu, yana fatan samun lada."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode hard until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ did not look back; Abu Bakr kept looking back. Then Suraqah’s horse sank into the ground up to its knees, and he fell."
msgstr "Ya yi gudu sosai har ya ji Annabi ﷺ yana karatu. Annabi ﷺ bai waiwaya ba; Abu Bakr kuwa yana yawan waiwaya. Sai dokin Suraqah ya nutse cikin ƙasa har gwiwoyinsa, shi kuma ya faɗi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Shaken, Suraqah begged them for a promise of safety and offered them provisions. They asked only, “Keep our whereabouts hidden.” ‘Amir wrote the promise on leather, and Suraqah rode back, turning every pursuer home."
msgstr "A firgice, Suraqah ya roƙe su su ba shi tabbacin tsira, kuma ya ba su guzuri. Abin da suka nema kawai shi ne: “Ka ɓoye inda muke.” ‘Amir ya rubuta masa wannan tabbaci a kan fata, Suraqah kuma ya koma a kan dokinsa, yana mai sa duk masu binsu su juya su koma gida."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah gave up the chase. They asked him to tell no one where they were, and he sent other searchers the wrong way."
msgstr "Suraqah ya daina binsu. Sun roƙe shi kada ya gaya wa kowa inda suke, sai ya karkatar da sauran masu nemansu zuwa wata hanya dabam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hungry and far from home, they stopped at the tent of a woman called Umm Ma‘bad. She had no food to give them."
msgstr "Suna jin yunwa kuma suna nesa da gida, sai suka tsaya a tantin wata mata mai suna Umm Ma‘bad. Ba ta da abincin da za ta ba su."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Her thin sheep had no milk. The Prophet ﷺ said Allah’s name and milked the sheep, and everyone drank!"
msgstr "Tunkiyarta siririya ba ta da nono. Annabi ﷺ ya ambaci sunan Allah ya kuma tatsa ta, sai kowa ya sha!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After they left, her husband came home. She told him of their guest: a shining face, and words like beads on a string."
msgstr "Bayan sun tafi, mijinta ya dawo gida. Ta ba shi labarin baƙonsu: fuskarsa mai haske ce, maganarsa kuma kamar ƙwayoyin lu’u-lu’u da aka jera a zare."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each morning the Ansar, the Muslims of Madinah, watched for him until the heat drove them in. Then a man on a fort saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Kowace safiya, Ansar, wato Musulman Madinah, suna sa ido don su gan shi har zafin rana ya sa su koma gida. Wata rana sai wani mutum a kan wani hasumiya ya ga matafiya sanye da fararen kaya, suna kyalli cikin zirin iska: “Ga wanda kuke jira!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him at Quba, a village just outside Madinah, resting under a palm with Abu Bakr. Most had never seen him, and greeted Abu Bakr, until the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr shaded him with his cloak."
msgstr "Sun same shi a Quba, wani ƙauye a wajen Madinah, yana hutawa a ƙarƙashin dabino tare da Abu Bakr. Yawancinsu ba su taɓa ganinsa ba, don haka suka gaishe da Abu Bakr, har sai da rana ta haska Annabi ﷺ, Abu Bakr kuma ya yi masa inuwa da mayafinsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Ali caught up with him there. He had stayed three days in Makkah to return what people had left in the Prophet’s ﷺ care. At Quba the Prophet ﷺ founded his mosque, and on a Friday he rode on towards Madinah."
msgstr "‘Ali ya same shi a wurin. Ya yi kwana uku a Makkah don mayar da kayayyakin da mutane suka ajiye a hannun Annabi ﷺ. A Quba Annabi ﷺ ya kafa masallacinsa, sannan a ranar Juma’a ya hau dabbarsa ya nufi Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last the Prophet ﷺ rode into Madinah on his camel. Everyone asked him to stay, but he let the camel choose the way."
msgstr "A ƙarshe Annabi ﷺ ya shiga Madinah a kan raƙuminsa. Kowa yana roƙonsa ya sauka a wurinsa, amma ya bar raƙumin ya zaɓi inda zai dosa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People climbed up high to see him. His camel knelt in a yard where dates were dried, and there he made his home."
msgstr "Mutane sun hau wurare masu tsawo don su gan shi. Raƙuminsa ya durƙusa a wani fili da ake shimfiɗa dabino don busarwa, a nan ne ya kafa gidansa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He prayed that Allah would make the Muslims love Madinah as much as Makkah, and even more."
msgstr "Ya roƙi Allah Ya sa Musulmai su ƙaunaci Madinah kamar yadda suke ƙaunar Makkah, har ma fiye da haka."

