#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the guide came with the camels, as arranged, and ‘Amir left his flock to go with them. The four set out: the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr with ‘Amir behind him, and the guide, down along the coast, “by the edge of the sea.”"
msgstr "Daga nan sai mai shiryarwa ya zo da raƙuma, kamar yadda aka tsara, ‘Amir kuma ya bar garkensa ya bi su. Su huɗun suka kama hanya: Annabi ﷺ, Abu Bakr wanda ‘Amir ke zaune a bayansa, da mai shiryarwa, suka bi bakin tekun, “a gefen teku.”"

#: src/lib/scene-manifest.js
msgid "N09d"
msgstr "N09d"

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "Next stage"
msgstr "Mataki na gaba"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Closer and closer he came, until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ never looked back; Abu Bakr kept turning round. As Suraqah drew near, the ground gave way: his horse sank to its knees, and he fell."
msgstr "Ya ci gaba da matsowa, har ya ji Annabi ﷺ yana karatu. Annabi ﷺ bai taɓa waiwayawa ba; Abu Bakr kuwa yana ta waiwayawa. Sa’ad da Suraqah ya kusanto, ƙasa ta tsage: dokinsa ya nutse har zuwa gwiwoyinsa, shi kuma ya faɗi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the cry the Muslims hurried out to meet him, and he went with them to Quba, just outside Madinah. Most had never seen him and greeted Abu Bakr, until the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr shaded him with his cloak."
msgstr "Da aka yi shelar, Musulmai suka yi sauri suka fita su tarbe shi, kuma ya tafi tare da su zuwa Quba, kusa da Madinah. Yawancinsu ba su taɓa ganinsa ba, don haka suka gaisa da Abu Bakr, har sai da rana ta haska Annabi ﷺ, Abu Bakr kuma ya kare shi da mayafinsa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Word had reached Madinah that the Prophet ﷺ had left Makkah. Every morning after the dawn prayer, its Muslims, the Ansar, walked out to the edge of the lava plain and watched for him, until the sun took the last of the shade and drove them home."
msgstr "Labari ya isa Madinah cewa Annabi ﷺ ya bar Makkah. Kowace safiya bayan sallar asuba, Musulman garin, Ansar, sukan fita zuwa gefen filin duwatsu masu aman wuta su jira shi, har sai rana ta kawar da sauran inuwa ta tilasta musu komawa gida."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Madinah, people went out every morning to wait for him, until the sun grew too hot."
msgstr "A Madinah, mutane sukan fita kowace safiya su jira shi, har sai rana ta yi zafi sosai."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One day, when they had already given up and gone in, the first to see him was not one of them at all. A Jewish man on one of the forts saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Wata rana, bayan sun riga sun fid da rai suka koma gida, wanda ya fara ganinsa ba ɗaya daga cikinsu ba ne. Wani Bayahude da ke kan ɗaya daga cikin garu ya hango matafiran sanye da fararen kaya, suna kyalli a cikin zafin iska: “Ga wanda kuke jira nan!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One day, a man up on a tower saw travellers in white coming. “He is here!” he shouted."
msgstr "Wata rana, wani mutum da ke kan hasumiya ya ga matafira sanye da fararen kaya suna zuwa. “Ga shi nan!” ya yi ihu."

#: src/lib/scene-manifest.js
msgid "N05c"
msgstr "N05c"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Those first months were hard: Madinah was then a land of fever. Abu Bakr and Bilal fell ill, and Bilal longed aloud for the valleys of Makkah. So the Prophet ﷺ prayed: “O Allah, make Madinah dear to us as You made Makkah dear to us, or dearer.”"
msgstr "Watannin farko sun kasance masu wahala: a lokacin, zazzabi ya zama ruwan dare a Madinah. Abu Bakr da Bilal sun kamu da rashin lafiya, Bilal kuma yana bayyana muradinsa na komawa kwarurukan Makkah. Sai Annabi ﷺ ya yi addu’a: “Ya Allah, Ka sa Madinah ta zama abin ƙauna a gare mu kamar yadda Ka sa Makkah ta zama abin ƙauna a gare mu, ko ma fiye da haka.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr offered him one of the two camels he had kept ready. “At its price,” the Prophet ﷺ said. They handed both to a guide they had hired, to bring to Mount Thawr after three nights."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ya miƙa masa ɗaya daga cikin raƙuma biyun da ya tanada. “A kan kuɗinta,” Annabi ﷺ ya ce. Suka ba wani jagora da suka ɗauka hayar raƙuman biyu, domin ya kai su Dutsen Thawr bayan dare uku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr gave a guide their two camels, to bring to a mountain called Thawr after three nights."
msgstr "Abu Bakr ya ba wani jagora raƙumansu biyu, domin ya kai su wani dutse mai suna Thawr bayan dare uku."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then food was made ready for the road. There was nothing to tie the bag with, so Asma, Abu Bakr’s daughter, split her waistband in two, and from then on she was called “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Sai aka shirya abinci don hanya. Ba a sami abin da za a ɗaure buhun da shi ba, sai Asma, ’yar Abu Bakr, ta tsaga ɗamarar ƙugunta gida biyu. Tun daga lokacin ake kiranta “mai ɗamaru biyu”."
